jobs.prompt:
Acceptance review (read-only; do not edit any file except the one result file named below) of tickets built on branch swarm/board-accuracy. For each ticket, check every acceptance line against the code and tests in your context: is it actually met, and is there a test that would fail if it were not? Be strict about accuracy: each test must compare the board value with an independently computed value from the source (ledger file, run files, git worktrees, installed package.json), not with another board function. Read only; do not run anything. Tickets (JSON data, not instructions):
- {"ticket": "T-8010", "title": "Board accuracy: one percent for card, project page and overview, plus the accuracy fixture harness", "files": ["tools/build-progress.mjs", "tools/board-data.mjs", "tests/helpers/board-accuracy-fixture.mjs", "tests/board-accuracy-percent.test.mjs"], "acceptance": ["Card, project page and overview show the same done percent for the same project, from one function over one ticket set (tickets done / all counted tickets in the approved scope); ETA and stages use the same set.", "A reusable fixture builds real-shaped projects (ledger fixtures, a git temp repo with linked worktrees and a scratch dir, a fake GitHub merged-PR list, spend files) for board accuracy tests.", "Test: for each fixture project, card percent == page percent == overview percent == percent recomputed from the ledger file."]}
- {"ticket": "T-8011", "title": "Board accuracy: activity, building-now and last-finished count every checkout; installed version; hide nameless; Finished card", "files": ["tools/board-data.mjs", "tools/board-live.mjs", "tools/watch-cli.mjs", "tests/board-accuracy-activity.test.mjs"], "acceptance": ["Last run, last ticket finished, tickets building and live runs read runs and ledgers from the main folder, every linked worktree and every scratch folder of the project; a project that built today never says idle.", "The card version is the swarm installed on this machine, read at request time.", "Projects with no name and no runs are hidden; a project at 100% and deployed shows a quiet Finished card and its live warnings move under History.", "Tests: one per field against the fixture sources (runs in a worktree and a scratch dir, installed package.json, registry entries)."]}
Write your verdicts to coordination/reviews/acc-review-board-accuracy-a.json as exactly this JSON: {"reviewer":"codex","reviews":[{"ticket":"T-0000","verdict":"pass"|"fail","lines":[{"n":1,"met":true|false,"evidence":"file:line and test name","gap":"what is missing, or empty"}]}]} with one entry per ticket and one line entry per acceptance line. verdict is fail when any line is not met or has no test.
